      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOUSE PARTY (6) enjoys a class drop off the Vicbred Super Series and will be race fit third up off a long spell. Won the only time she attempted this distance and finds a much more winnable assignment. KING BALDWIN (4) scored on debut at Cranbourne before tackling a Vicbred heat at his latest appearance at Melton. Better placed and has upside. RYTA (3) led from this barrier and stuck on for a respectable third when resuming at Stawell. Won his lone second-up attempt so should be improved and also scored the only time he attempted this circuit and distance. EXOTIC CHESTER (2) is first up for 12 weeks but was readied with a trial win and didn't miss the top-four in his maiden campaign, highlighted by a win here. Draws for a good return.",
